# .gitattributes - tells Git how to treat the line endings of files
#
# Windows and Linux end each line of text with different invisible characters
# ("line endings"): Windows uses two (CRLF), Linux and macOS use one (LF). On
# Windows, Git may change files to the Windows style when it writes them into
# the project folder. The hooks write their files (the README tree, the
# progress pages, the notes) with LF on every computer. This line keeps every
# text file in LF everywhere too, so a file a hook rewrites never looks
# changed only because of its line endings. "text=auto" lets Git find out by
# itself which files are text; pictures and other binary files are not touched.
# A line starting with "#" is a comment for people only.
* text=auto eol=lf
